course: dictionary
lesson: 13644
title: Inexperienced
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Inexperienced means you have not had much practice, so you do not yet know much about doing something. «The inexperienced driver drove very slowly around the corner.» The word slowly is a clue: a new driver has not done much driving, so they go carefully.
explain: Look at the words near it to find out what someone is inexperienced at or in. «She is inexperienced at baking, so she followed the recipe step by step.» The word at tells you the skill: baking.
explain: Being inexperienced is normal, because everyone starts as a beginner. «Every new player is a bit inexperienced at first, and that is fine.» Inexperienced is not a bad word; it simply means new to something.
fact: Inexperienced means not having much knowledge or skill because you have not done something much.
fact: Inexperienced is an adjective, so it describes a person or thing, as in «an inexperienced teacher».
fact: Inexperienced is the opposite of experienced, which means you have done something many times.
fact: Inexperienced swimmers and climbers should always stay with an adult or instructor.
fact: In a story, an inexperienced hero often learns and grows as the story goes on.
exercise: «The inexperienced swimmer stayed close to the instructor.» What does inexperienced mean? | *Not having much skill because she has not done it much | Afraid of the sea forever | Very fast and strong in the water | Happy to swim far away alone
exercise: «He is inexperienced in fixing bikes, so he asked his dad for help.» What is he inexperienced in? | Riding fast down hills | Reading maps | Asking his dad for help | *Fixing bikes
exercise: Mia says, «I am young and inexperienced, but I want to try.» What does inexperienced tell us about Mia? | She is a famous expert | *She has not done this much yet | She does not want to try | She has done this a hundred times
test: «The inexperienced climber roped herself to her guide before the steep part.» Why would an inexperienced climber stay with a guide? | *Because she has not climbed much and needs safety | Because guides are not allowed to climb | Because she is an expert who wants to show off | Because the mountain is flat
test: Which word is the opposite of inexperienced? | *Experienced | Young | Nervous | Beginner
exam: In a story, «The inexperienced knight was scared, but he learned something new on every quest.» What does this tell us about the knight? | *He will grow more skilled as the story goes on | He is a famous, skilled knight from the start | He will never learn anything | He has fought a hundred battles already
